    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but is \"finding new meaning\" just another way of saying we're just decorating our cages? if the universe is actually indifferent, then all this effort to \"find purpose\" feels like a cope. it seems more intellectually honest to just admit that the agency to stop participating is the only real choice we actually have. why is it considered \"unsettling\" rather than just a logical conclusion of autonomy?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
